       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the maximum labeled daily dose for adults, which is 3,200 mg/day under physician supervision. The usual limit for a single dose is 800 mg. At this level the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up sharply, and there is no added analgesic or anti-inflammatory benefit.\n\nHere are some likely intended orders:\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), a common anti-inflammatory dose\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum\n- **1600 mg/day total**, divided into some other schedule\n\nTell me which dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that and give me a clinical rationale to put in the order note. I'd still want to flag it before entering something that far over the maximum."
